<title>BELGIUM: Zaire cobalt supplies still flowing - Union Miniere.</title>
<headline>Zaire cobalt supplies still flowing - Union Miniere.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-04-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The chief executive officer of Union Miniere Karel Vinck said on Monday that cobalt supplies from Zaire were still flowing despite advances by rebel forces.</p>
<p>&quot;We don't see any negative impact yet on the operations we have there and in particular the Kosombo cobalt mine,&quot; Vinck told Reuters after speaking at a Metal Bulletin zinc conference.</p>
<p>Vinck said that rail transport routes through South Africa were still running. - Brussels newsroom: +32 2 287-6830</p>
</text>
